60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: The options are A: Paid Allocation, B: Shared Racks, and C: Annual Lottery. Let’s discuss.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: I lean toward B. Shared racks mean no one owns a spot, so no one gets stuck in the rain or the shoving match.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"- **May**: @Shizue, wait. Option A brings in cash. Our ledger is empty, and the station park costs 2,600 yen. We need that income.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,George,,"- **George**: @May, I caution against A. The handover file shows three hours monthly for current tasks. Adding billing risks the role lapsing again.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @May, I agree with George. The sticker register showed people want to pay, but the neighbor’s block fell apart under the weight of it.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: @Mio, the neighbor’s block had arrears. If we charge, we risk the same social fracture. I prefer B’s simplicity.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Misaki, I agree. Shared racks remove the ownership disputes that caused those nine complaints. It’s the kindest path.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"- **May**: @George, but without that income, we can’t fix the rain damage. We’d just be sharing the misery, not solving it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,George,,"- **George**: @May, you’re right about the rain. But B’s racks need greasing twice a year. That’s a small, shared task, not a monthly burden.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @George, twice a year is manageable. I vote for B. It’s simple, fair, and won’t break the bank or the friendships.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: @Mio, agreed. B avoids the social fracture of A and the rigidity of C. I’m with you on B.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Mio, I’m with you. B feels the most peaceful and sustainable for all of us.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"- **May**: @Mio, I’m still stuck. If we can’t afford the racks, B is just a dream. I need that income.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,George,,"- **George**: @May, the ledger is empty, but B requires no monthly billing. We only need a one-time levy for the racks, which is far less than the station park.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @May, a one-time levy is easier to swallow than a monthly bill. I’m sticking with B.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: @May, I understand your worry, but a one-time levy is safer than monthly billing. I vote B.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @May, I understand your worry, but a one-time levy is safer than monthly billing. I vote B.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"- **May**: @George, a one-time levy is better than monthly billing. I’ll go with B, but we must fund the racks properly.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,George,,"- **George**: Agreed. A one-time levy is manageable. I vote B, provided we schedule the greasing.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @May, I’m glad you’re on board. I vote B too. Let’s get those racks installed!","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
